@translation unitary en project
@unit 1
@span i 1 - ii 16
For Ninŋirsu, the powerful warrior of Enlil, his master, Gudea, ruler of Lagaš, the builder of Ninŋirsu's E-ninnu, built Ninŋirsu, his master's E-ŋidru, the temple of seven niches, the temple whose scepter takes precedence, (and) for which Ninŋirsu decided a good fate. Ninŋirsu dispatches the joyful bridewealth of Bau, the child of An, his beloved spouse, from this (temple). (Gudea's) personal god, Ninŋešzida follows them, (and) Gudea, ruler of Lagaš, @?escorts?@ them from Ŋirsu to Iri-kug @?to congratulate (on the occasion)?@.

@unit 2
@span ii 17 - iii 4
In this very year he transported diorite from the mountains of Magan, (and) fashioned his statue from it. 

@unit 3
@span iii 5 - iv 20
At the turn of the year, at the festival of Bau, when the bridewealth is to be presented, the bridewealth for Bau consisted of these in the former, old temple: uz-bird, 7 cranes, 15 geese, 60 small birds in strings of 15, 60 @suḫurtun-carps in strings of 30, 30 @gun turnip, 7 @gun marsh reed, 60 @gun @manu wood.

@unit 4
@span iv 21 - vi 19
After Gudea, ruler of Lagaš built his beloved temple, the E-ninnu, for Ninŋirsu, his master, (and) built her beloved temple, the E-tarsirsir, for Bau, his lady, the bridewealth for Bau consists of these in the new temple, increased by Gudea, ruler of Lagaš, the temple-builder: uz bird, 7 cranes, 10 geese, 7 @izi-birds, 60 small birds in strings of 15, 60 @suḫurtun-carps in strings of 30, 40 @gun turnip, 7 @gun marsh reed, 60 @gun @manu wood.




